For ease of exposition, the reference position of the UPA is assumed to be at the origin.
Denote the distance between the BS and the $k$-th user as $r_k$, and represent the position of the $k$-th user as $\mathbf{q}_k=\left[r_k\Phi_k, r_k\Psi_k,r_k\Omega_k \right]^T\in \mathbb{R} ^{3\times 1}$ with $\Phi_k=\text{sin}\vartheta_k \text{sin}\phi_k$, $\Psi_k=\text{cos}\vartheta_k$, and $\Omega_k=\text{sin}\vartheta_k \text{cos}\phi_k$, where $\vartheta_k\in \left[ -\frac{\pi}{2},\frac{\pi}{2}\right]$ and $\phi_k\in [0,\pi]$ denote the elevation angle and azimuth angle of the $k$-th user with respect to the origin of the coordinate system, respectively, for $k=1,...,K$.  

