We now present a method for constructing an important
space called
the \defn{homology cover}\footnote{
We use the term ``homology cover'' to refer to the one-dimensional $\mathbb{Z}_2$-homology cover
of the annulus.
}.
Take the specified path between the two boundaries
(see \cref{fig:homology-cover-construction-a})
and slice it open
(see \cref{fig:homology-cover-construction-b}).
Then, create a second copy of the sliced annulus,
and glue them together
in a way that matches up the orientations of the sliced ends
(see \cref{fig:homology-cover-construction-c}).

