\begin{equation}
\Big| -B_j \Big|_{\fermn} = 
\Big| \bar{B_j} - \left( \sum_{i=0}^{n-1} b_{j,i} 2^i \right) \Big|_{\fermn} = 
\bar{B_j} +2 .
\label{eqn-notbj}\end{equation}
Eqn \eqref{eqn-notbj} indicates the correction constant equal to 2, 
which must be added mod \fermn{} to the final result. 

Basically, Eqns \eqref{x-blocks-ferm:b} and \eqref{eqn-notbj} 
can be used as a starting point to design the residue generator mod \fermn{} 
with D1 output. 
