As a first numerical experiment, we consider the elliptic model problem \cref{eq:weakform} with the coefficient $A_1$ shown in \cref{fig:ellipticcoefficient} (left). The coefficient is piecewise constant on a uniform Cartesian grid $\mathcal{T}_\epsilon$ with mesh size $\epsilon = 2^{-7}$. For all elements whose midpoints lie within a distance of $4\epsilon$ from a given parabola, the coefficient is set to a value of 2. In all other elements, the coefficient values are sampled independently from a uniform distribution on the interval $[0.1, 1]$.
