\subsection{Soundness}
In this section, we prove the soundness of the $\OC$-calculus with respect to the denotational semantics (Theorem~\ref{thm:soundness}). We begin by introducing the notion of substitution, which plays a key role in the proof. This is done through two lemmas: one for the substitution of a non-linear variable (Lemma~\ref{lem:nonlinearsubstitution}) and another for the substitution of a linear variable (Lemma~\ref{lem:linearsubstitution}).

The proofs of these lemmas rely not only on the properties established in previous sections, but also on several technical lemmas, which are stated and proved in Appendix~\ref{proof:technical}.

