We can observe that, by setting $\beta = \Theta (T^{-3/4})$ and $\eta = \Theta (T^{-1/4})$ in Theorem \ref{Theorem_UpperBoundCError}, the C-error converges to the conflict-resolving direction at rate $\mathcal{O}(T^{-1/4})$.

