Substituting the upper bounds of gradients assumed in Theorem \ref{Theorem_UpperBoundGError}, we can also prove that $\epsilon$ is bounded by a constant, given by $\epsilon^2 \le \frac{4U^2T}{D}$. Finally, by substituting this bound of $\epsilon$ into the upper bound of $\cE_G$, we can obtain the result.
\end{IEEEproof}

