\paragraph{Graph Analysis.}
The concept of \emph{blocking sets} is also known as vertex cuts or vertex separators in graph theory: given a start and an end vertex, a blocking set is a set of vertices (without the start and end vertices) such that the end vertex is not reachable from the start vertex without passing a member of the blocking set. The identification of blocking sets has numerous applications, for example in VLSI design and cybersecurity.
