%%%%%%%%%%%%%%\subsection*{Areas for Improvement for AI Tools}

%%%%%%%%%%%%%%One of the main ways AI tools for software development need to improve is in the software developer experience. Given that these tools are most reliably used by an experienced software engineer (rather than replacing engineers entirely), the process could be drastically improved by a tool with a far smoother workflow. One of the main obstacles within this workflow is having to use separate tools in separate windows throughout the process, for example copying code from ChatGPT into an IDE and copying error logs back in to ChatGPT. Therefore, a single tool to integrate all the processes and functionalities required for the development cycle into a user-friendly experience is necessary. GPT Pilot serves as a good example of this: automatically writing code into files, the AI always being up to date with the current version of code updating the user on what processes are being carried out, asking for feedback and input from the user and asking the user to test functionalities. However, GPT Pilot is not without its flaws which can be improved on as outlined in the rest of this section. 


%%%%%%%%%%%%%%\bigskip

%%%%%%%%%%%%%%As shown by disorganised code and increasing response time in approach B, there is need for greater emphasis on planning at the beginning of the project. Furthermore, the tools used could benefit from continuous emphasis on ensuring the code adheres to the plan and potentially updating the software architecture plan when new features are proposed if necessary. This may also mean that these tools ought to be trained specifically on expert advice on software architecture planning.

%%%%%%%%%%%%%%\bigskip

%%%%%%%%%%%%%%The tools could also be improved by implementing the rest of the DevOps process. Continuous testing (generation and execution of tests), integration, deployment, evaluation and feedback could feasibly be automated  and integrated into the same tool, which would execute this process for every new feature developed. For example, when a new feature is implemented it is automatically tested by both the user and unit tests, with error and debugging logs automatically being relayed to the AI.

%%%%%%%%%%%%%%\bigskip

%%%%%%%%%%%%%%Another potential use of AI could be in functionality testing. Rather than having the user manually run tests and giving natural language feedback, AI could be used to run the game automatically, execute necessary commands (e.g. press keys), and process the outputs (visual, audio, or error logs). While current AI tools are not yet at this level and human intervention still may be necessary to ensure that the AI tests are valid, this could potentially greatly reduce the primary consumer of time and effort in the software development process: debugging and fixing faulty code.

%%%%%%%%%%%%%%\bigskip

%%%%%%%%%%%%%%Furthermore, the current scope of AI tools is entirely based off a single developer, so there is a need for AI tools which can be collaboratively by a  software engineering team. This would need to implement version control as well as keeping the different instances of AI in the loop about different plans and versions. It could also potentially use AI tools to analyse merge requests.

%%%%%%%%%%%%%%\bigskip

%%%%%%%%%%%%%%As mentioned, there exists a need for great improvement in the use of AI tools for generating graphics. The workflow for the simple graphics generated in this project was very tedious, so for high quality graphics it is possible that a specialised, dedicated tool will be needed. 

%%%%%%%%%%%%%%\bigskip
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%\subsection*{Guidance on Adopting AI Tools into DevOps}

%%%%%%%%%%%%%%With the current state of AI tools, teams or individuals looking to develop software can significantly benefit in efficiency by making use of AI tools. However, it should be noted that with the current state of AI tools, especially for higher complexity and higher importance software projects, AI tools are not to be relied on and require control and oversight by a software engineer.

%%%%%%%%%%%%%%When adopting AI tools into software development, we can consider its use in each stage of the DevOps process. AI chatbots such as ChatGPT have been shown to be able to generate adequate requirements and software architecture for this project, but further research is needed on the extent to which it can intelligently plan complex software. Therefore, for higher-stakes software projects AI tools can be used to save time in the planning stage and provide suggestions, but should be managed by an experienced software architect to ensure a solid foundational plan for the software. Taking this into account, a team could work with the consumer to outline the requirements for the software. The AI could then propose a software architecture plan which the development team would review and scrutinise before settling on.

%%%%%%%%%%%%%%AI code generation tools have been relatively effective at generating working code when given sufficient context and specific instructions. Therefore, an experienced software engineer could, possibly using AI tools, divide a project into manageable chunks and write specific documentation for each section outlining what functionalities the code should perform, in what way and following what conventions and standards. Then taking each chunk at a time, code and relevant tests could be generated then integrated together and tested as a whole package. However, as shown especially by approach C in this study, there are bound to be issues with the code in integration and successfully running tests. An experienced software engineer or team is required to oversee the process and attempt to work with the AI tools to debug when issues inevitably arise. 

%%%%%%%%%%%%%%As for the rest of the DevOps processes (continuous integration and deployment, operations and feedback) the AI tools on the market were not tested in this study, so a judgement on their efficacy cannot be made. 

%%%%%%%%%%%%%%\bigskip

%%%%%%%%%%%%%%Another point to make is that for individuals with lacking experience software development and programming, AI tools can be very effective tools at speeding up the process. AI tools can be a significant time-saving tool in the planning and bulk-code writing processes. Therefore, for an individual looking to develop a software package, AI tools like those used in this study can speed up the process and save the user from spending extensive amounts of time researching and planning. However, rather than shifting all the time and effort into debugging issues with AI-generated code, a better approach would be to use AI assistants for help when struggling (e.g. fixing errors or providing suggestions for how to implement a feature) and to use code generation tools (such as copilot) when the user is clear on how they want to implement a feature. In this way the user doesn't become reliant on AI-generated code and is able to retain control of the source code and the project. 

