To improve QoS of co-locating models, spatial partitioning allocates distinct portions of GPU internal compute resources to kernels within a request, lessening contention. However, even the state-of-the-art inference servers employing spatial partitioning~\cite{classsearch, warperslicer, improvedscale, KRISP, elasticroom} still suffer from the following key limitations. 

