\smallskip
\noindent\textbf{Fairness among Workers for Energy Efficiency:}
In co-located scenarios where multiple workers handle inference requests concurrently, our optimizer must ensure fairness while maximizing overall GPU utilization. This fairness is critical because disparate completion times among workers lead to idling CUs, wasting energy due to the lack of CU-level power gating as explained in Sec.~\ref{sec:gpu_energy}. To address this issue, we associate one identically weighted objective function per worker, where each objective function aims to minimize the execution time of that worker's kernels. 
