Thus, the $n$-th letter is influential. Contradiction.
\end{proof}

\begin{myclaim}\label{clm:reading-not-from-epsilon-decreasing-rank}
Let $L\subseteq \Sigma^\omega$ and $x\in\Sigma^*$. 
If $\letterrank_L(x,|x|)=d$ then $\letterrank_L(zx,|zx|)\leq d$ for all $z\in \Sigma^*$.
