\section{Conclusions}
We present MoFE-Time, a novel time series forecasting model that leverages frequency domain analysis networks alongside a MoE architecture. By integrating a frequency domain analysis module within the expert networks and combining it with temporal features of signals, the model enhances its ability to learn the intrinsic properties of time series. The training architecture employs a pre-training phase followed by fine-tuning, supplemented by the integration of the RevIN method, which collectively enhances the model's predictive capabilities. %The training architecture, which utilizes pre-training followed by finetuing, along with the incorporation of the RevIN method, significantly boosts the model's predictive performance. 
MoFE-Time has achieved new state-of-the-art performance on a few benchmarks, and is especially robust on a proprietary dataset focusing on NEV sales, substantiating its effectiveness in real-world commercial applications forecasting scenarios, thus providing a valuable tool for business intelligence and operational decision-making.%Besides, To assess the practical efficacy of MoFE-Time in commercial applications, we have developed a proprietary dataset focusing on NEV sales,

%To verify the effectiveness of our model in real-world commercial environments, we collected and constructed the proprietary NEV-sales dataset and evaluated the performance of the MoFE-Time model on it. Experimental results demonstrate that our model achieved state-of-the-art performance in terms of overall accuracy, thereby validating the effectiveness of the MoFE-Time model.

