\begin{abstract}
    We study the safety problem for the next-generation access control (NGAC) model. We show that under mild assumptions it is $\coNP$-complete, and under further realistic assumptions we give an algorithm for the safety problem that significantly outperforms naive brute force search. 
    We also show that real-world examples of mutually exclusive attributes lead to nearly worst-case behavior of our algorithm.
\end{abstract}

