Therefore,
\[
M^\pm(m,n)=C^\pm(m,n)+D(m,n). 
\] The proof for $M^+(m,n)$ is similar except that we only need to account for the $n$ flips $r^+_i$ with $1\leq i\leq n$.  Therefore, in this case the diagonal entries should be half of $D(m,n)$ and blocks of the form $C^\pm(m,n)$ are of the form $C^+(m,n)$.
\end{proof}

