    Since within the matrix $C^\pm(m)$ there are only two non-zero entries of one in each row and that the entries in $\vl$ are in ``blocks'' of length $m$, we can consider the product of $C^\pm(m,n)$ with $\vl$ ``block-wise'' where the analogous ``scalar'' multiplication results in double the entries of $\vl$ in the resulting product vector $C^\pm(m,n) \vl$. Similarly, we can multiply ``block-wise'' with $D(m,n)$ and $\vl$. We now examine the cases based on the values of $1 \leq j \leq n$.

