\subsection{Parameter Tuning}
We analyze the polygon approximation of the feasible operating region (\(\mathcal{F}\)) of the sub-transmission system, which is represented by 36 vertices corresponding to a resolution of \(10^\circ\). The edges of \(\mathcal{F}\) are defined by the active constraints that vary across different regions of the operating points \(\mathbf{s}_{\text{PCC}}\) on the PQ-plane. To evaluate the controller performance, we consider two parameter sets with different scalar gains \(\alpha\) and a fixed weighting matrix \(G\), as shown in \autoref{tab:ofo_tuning}.

