\subsection{Comparision with TC-GNN SpMM}
\label{sec:tc-gnn}
Besides Nvidia's cuSparse Blocked-ELL SpMM, the only other effort to use tensor cores for SpMM (to our knowledge) is TC-GNN\cite{wang2021tc}. TC-GNN implements Graph Neural Networks (GNN), where SpMM is a dominant computational component. However, the SpMM implementation within TC-GNN is highly integrated with Pytorch and no API is available for directly executing the internal SpMM implementation to perform a direct comparison with  cuTeSpMM. Although we were not able perform a direct experimental comparison with TC-GNN's SpMM implementtaion,  we report the speedup achieved by cuTeSpMM over cuSparse Blocked-ELL on five specific sparse matrices reported by Wang et al. \cite{wang2021tc}, using a similar GPU (they used an Nvidia RTX3090, which is quite similar in overall performance to the Nvidia RTX A6000 we use as one of two GPUs for our experimets). Table~\ref{tab:geomean-1} shows that the achieved speedup of cuTeSpMM over cuSparse Blocked-ELL is very much higher than the speedup reported by Wang et al. \cite{wang2021tc}.

