To show that the real fibers can be glued to sections, we need a stronger condition in morphism.
\begin{definition}
	%Let $X$, $Y$ be affine $k$-varieties and $\pi: X\to Y$ is a dominant $k$-morphism. Suppose there are closed immersions $i_X:X\to \mathbb{A}_k^{n+1},i_Y:Y\to \mathbb{A}_k^n$ making the following diagram commute:
