%\section{Conclusion}\label{sect-conclusion}
%In this paper, we study the geometric fiber classification problem for morphisms of varieties over a field of characteristic 0, and a new theory of Cylindrical Algebraic Decomposition from a geometric view is established in this paper. The new theory is based on a constructive version of Grothendieck's Generic Freeness Lemma and a parametric version of Hermite Quadratic Form. Our new theory provides novel insights into the classical theory of Cylindrical Algebraic Decomposition, since the classical theory can also be explained by the new one. We hope that the geometric view can pave the way for a deeper understanding of cylindrical algebraic decomposition and shed some light on the development of faster algorithms. In fact, it is already shown in this paper that, the geometric theory is directly applicable to taking constraints into consideration and a huge saving in computation is observed.

 %We related the construction of cylindrical algebraic decomposition to the study of geometric fibers of a finite free morphism between $R$-varieties, and a geometric theory of cylindrical algebraic decomposition is established in this paper. As a result, an efficient algorithm for cylindrical algebraic decomposition is developed in this paper. Experiments showed that our algorithm achieves better performance than the existing methods.

