\subsection{Preliminary results}
Before establishing the main results, some useful assumptions and preliminary results are introduced below.
\begin{assumption}\label{theassumptionofreward}
In the NMARL problem, the reward for each agent $i\in\mathcal{N}$ is uniformly bounded, i.e., there exist a constant $R_{0}$ such that $|r_{i}(\bm{z})|\leq R_{0}$ for all $\bm{z}\in\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{A}$.
\end{assumption}
%{\color{blue}For any joint policy $\bm{\pi}$, define
