There exists constants $L>0$ and $\sigma_{\xi}>0$ such that $\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}J(\bm{\pi}_{\bm{\theta}})$ is $L$-Lipschitz continuous and $\mathbb{E}_{\sigma_{k}}[\|\xi_{i,k}\|^{2}_{2}]\leq\frac{\sigma^{2}_{\xi}}{|\mathcal{B}|N}$ for all $i\in\mathcal{N}$ and $k=0,\cdots,K-1$.
